<tag>
<description><![CDATA[The Accordion is a container component that displays contents in a stacked format.<p>For more information, see the <a href="http://wiki.icefaces.org/display/ICE/Accordion">Accordion Wiki Documentation</a>.<hr><table border='1' cellpadding='3' cellspacing='0' width='100%'><tr bgcolor='#CCCCFF' class='TableHeadingColor'><td colspan='3'><font size='+2'><b>Client Events</b></font></td></tr><tr><td><b>Name</b></td><td><b>Description</b></td><td><b>Supported classes for argument</b></td><tr><tr><td>panechange</td><td>Fired when the active accordion pane is changed (default event).</td><td>javax.faces.event.AjaxBehaviorEvent</td></tr></table><i>Client events can be used with Client Behaviors and the ace:ajax tag.</i><br>]]></description>
<name>accordion</name>
<tag-class>org.icefaces.ace.component.accordion.AccordionTag</tag-class>
<body-content>JSP</body-content>
<attribute>
<description><![CDATA[Index of the active pane. Default = '0'.]]></description>
<name>activeIndex</name>
<required>no</required>
<rtexprvalue>true</rtexprvalue>
<type>int</type>
</attribute>
<attribute>
<description><![CDATA[When enabled, pane with highest content is used to calculate the height. Default = 'true'.]]></description>
<name>autoHeight</name>
<required>no</required>
<rtexprvalue>true</rtexprvalue>
<type>boolean</type>
</attribute>
<attribute>
<description><![CDATA[Using an EL expression, bind the component reference to a bean property, so that the component may be accessed in the bean.]]></description>
<name>binding</name>
<required>no</required>
<rtexprvalue>true</rtexprvalue>
<type>javax.el.ValueExpression</type>
</attribute>
<attribute>
<description><![CDATA[<strong>Deprecated</strong>. Defines if activating a dynamic pane should load the contents from server again. (This attribute is now deprecated. Every pane change will produce a request, and the contents of the panes will be updated if they differ from previous content.) Default = 'true'.]]></description>
<name>cache</name>
<required>no</required>
<rtexprvalue>true</rtexprvalue>
<type>boolean</type>
</attribute>
<attribute>
<description><![CDATA[Defines if accordion can be collapsed all together. Default = 'false'.]]></description>
<name>collapsible</name>
<required>no</required>
<rtexprvalue>true</rtexprvalue>
<type>boolean</type>
</attribute>
<attribute>
<description><![CDATA[Disables or enables the accordion. Default = 'false'.]]></description>
<name>disabled</name>
<required>no</required>
<rtexprvalue>true</rtexprvalue>
<type>boolean</type>
</attribute>
<attribute>
<description><![CDATA[<strong>Deprecated</strong>. Defines the toggle mode. (This attribute is now deprecated. Every pane change will produce a request, and the contents of the panes will be updated if they differ from previous content.) Default = 'false'.]]></description>
<name>dynamic</name>
<required>no</required>
<rtexprvalue>true</rtexprvalue>
<type>boolean</type>
</attribute>
<attribute>
<description><![CDATA[Effect to use when toggling the panes. Default = 'slide'.]]></description>
<name>effect</name>
<required>no</required>
<rtexprvalue>true</rtexprvalue>
<type>java.lang.String</type>
</attribute>
<attribute>
<description><![CDATA[Client side event to toggle the panes.]]></description>
<name>event</name>
<required>no</required>
<rtexprvalue>true</rtexprvalue>
<type>java.lang.String</type>
</attribute>
<attribute>
<description><![CDATA[When enabled, accordion fills the height of its parent container. Default = 'false'.]]></description>
<name>fillSpace</name>
<required>no</required>
<rtexprvalue>true</rtexprvalue>
<type>boolean</type>
</attribute>
<attribute>
<description><![CDATA[The component identifier for this component. This value must be unique within the closest parent component that is a naming container.]]></description>
<name>id</name>
<required>no</required>
<rtexprvalue>true</rtexprvalue>
<type>java.lang.String</type>
</attribute>
<attribute>
<description><![CDATA[Server side listener to invoke when active pane changes]]></description>
<name>paneChangeListener</name>
<required>no</required>
<rtexprvalue>true</rtexprvalue>
<type>javax.el.MethodExpression</type>
</attribute>
<attribute>
<description><![CDATA[Return true if this component (and its children) should be rendered during the Render Response phase of the request processing lifecycle. Default = 'true'.]]></description>
<name>rendered</name>
<required>no</required>
<rtexprvalue>true</rtexprvalue>
<type>boolean</type>
</attribute>
<attribute>
<description><![CDATA[Inline style of the container element.]]></description>
<name>style</name>
<required>no</required>
<rtexprvalue>true</rtexprvalue>
<type>java.lang.String</type>
</attribute>
<attribute>
<description><![CDATA[Style class of the container element.]]></description>
<name>styleClass</name>
<required>no</required>
<rtexprvalue>true</rtexprvalue>
<type>java.lang.String</type>
</attribute>
<attribute>
<description><![CDATA[Name of the widget to access client side api]]></description>
<name>widgetVar</name>
<required>no</required>
<rtexprvalue>true</rtexprvalue>
<type>java.lang.String</type>
</attribute>
</tag>
<tag>
<description><![CDATA[<p>Renders a hidden panel with controls to configure column features. The table whose columns are to be configured is targeted with the 'for' attribute. The location of the button to reveal this panel is configured via the 'type' attribute.</p><p>The table config panel renders three buttons, a checkmark which submits changes, a crossout that closes without submitting changes, and a trashcan, that closes and resets the column properties configurable via the table config panel to an unconfigured state. </p><p>For more information, see the <a href="http://wiki.icefaces.org/display/ICE/TableConfigPanel">TableConfigPanel Wiki Documentation</a>.</p><hr><table border='1' cellpadding='3' cellspacing='0' width='100%'><tr bgcolor='#CCCCFF' class='TableHeadingColor'><td colspan='3'><font size='+2'><b>Client Events</b></font></td></tr><tr><td><b>Name</b></td><td><b>Description</b></td><td><b>Supported classes for argument</b></td><tr><tr><td>open</td><td>Fired when the TableConfigPanel is shown.</td><td>javax.faces.event.AjaxBehaviorEvent</td></tr><tr><td>submit</td><td>Fired when the TableConfigPanel submits its changes and closes.</td><td>javax.faces.event.AjaxBehaviorEvent</td></tr><tr><td>cancel</td><td>Fired when the TableConfigPanel cancel its changes and closes.</td><td>javax.faces.event.AjaxBehaviorEvent</td></tr><tr><td>trash</td><td>Fired when the TableConfigPanel clears out it's changes and closes.</td><td>javax.faces.event.AjaxBehaviorEvent</td></tr></table><i>Client events can be used with Client Behaviors and the ace:ajax tag.</i><br>]]></description>
<name>tableConfigPanel</name>
<tag-class>org.icefaces.ace.component.tableconfigpanel.TableConfigPanelTag</tag-class>
<body-content>JSP</body-content>
<attribute>
<description><![CDATA[Using an EL expression, bind the component reference to a bean property, so that the component may be accessed in the bean.]]></description>
<name>binding</name>
<required>no</required>
<rtexprvalue>true</rtexprvalue>
<type>javax.el.ValueExpression</type>
</attribute>
<attribute>
<description><![CDATA[Enable the configuration of column headerText properties.]]></description>
<name>columnNameConfigurable</name>
<required>no</required>
<rtexprvalue>true</rtexprvalue>
<type>boolean</type>
</attribute>
<attribute>
<description><![CDATA[Enable the configuration of column order.]]></description>
<name>columnOrderingConfigurable</name>
<required>no</required>
<rtexprvalue>true</rtexprvalue>
<type>boolean</type>
</attribute>
<attribute>
<description><![CDATA[Enable the configuration of column sorting priority and directions.]]></description>
<name>columnSortingConfigurable</name>
<required>no</required>
<rtexprvalue>true</rtexprvalue>
<type>boolean</type>
</attribute>
<attribute>
<description><![CDATA[Enable the configuration of column visibility.]]></description>
<name>columnVisibilityConfigurable</name>
<required>no</required>
<rtexprvalue>true</rtexprvalue>
<type>boolean</type>
</attribute>
<attribute>
<description><![CDATA[Defines a CSS selector of a TableConfigPanel subregion used as the handle when dragging the panel.]]></description>
<name>dragHandle</name>
<required>no</required>
<rtexprvalue>true</rtexprvalue>
<type>java.lang.String</type>
</attribute>
<attribute>
<description><![CDATA[Defines the component ID of the DataTable this ConfigPanel manipulates.]]></description>
<name>for</name>
<required>no</required>
<rtexprvalue>true</rtexprvalue>
<type>java.lang.String</type>
</attribute>
<attribute>
<description><![CDATA[Enable to hide columns with configurable property set to false, rather than render them with a disabled style. Default = 'false'.]]></description>
<name>hideDisabledRows</name>
<required>no</required>
<rtexprvalue>true</rtexprvalue>
<type>boolean</type>
</attribute>
<attribute>
<description><![CDATA[The component identifier for this component. This value must be unique within the closest parent component that is a naming container.]]></description>
<name>id</name>
<required>no</required>
<rtexprvalue>true</rtexprvalue>
<type>java.lang.String</type>
</attribute>
<attribute>
<description><![CDATA[Defines the column to render the 'launch' panel button in when using the 'in-col-left' or 'in-col-right' type options.]]></description>
<name>inColumnId</name>
<required>no</required>
<rtexprvalue>true</rtexprvalue>
<type>java.lang.String</type>
</attribute>
<attribute>
<description><![CDATA[Define if viewing this panel disables the rest of the application from input. Default = 'false'.]]></description>
<name>modal</name>
<required>no</required>
<rtexprvalue>true</rtexprvalue>
<type>java.lang.Boolean</type>
</attribute>
<attribute>
<description><![CDATA[Define the distance in pixels from left boundary of the CSS positioning bounding parent. If undefiend the panel is positioned offset slightly from the target DataTable.]]></description>
<name>offsetLeft</name>
<required>no</required>
<rtexprvalue>true</rtexprvalue>
<type>java.lang.Integer</type>
</attribute>
<attribute>
<description><![CDATA[Define the distance in pixels from top boundary of the CSS positioning bounding parent. If undefiend the panel is positioned offset slightly from the target DataTable.]]></description>
<name>offsetTop</name>
<required>no</required>
<rtexprvalue>true</rtexprvalue>
<type>java.lang.Integer</type>
</attribute>
<attribute>
<description><![CDATA[Return true if this component (and its children) should be rendered during the Render Response phase of the request processing lifecycle. Default = 'true'.]]></description>
<name>rendered</name>
<required>no</required>
<rtexprvalue>true</rtexprvalue>
<type>boolean</type>
</attribute>
<attribute>
<description><![CDATA[Defines the display mode for the 'open' control panel button. Available options: first-col, last-col, in-col-right, in-col-left Default = 'first-col'.]]></description>
<name>type</name>
<required>no</required>
<rtexprvalue>true</rtexprvalue>
<type>java.lang.String</type>
</attribute>
</tag>
<tag>
<description><![CDATA[Enables an Id-specified component to be moved via dragging. Draggable component can cause events on droppable ones.<p>For more information, see the <a href="http://wiki.icefaces.org/display/ICE/Draggable">Draggable Wiki Documentation</a>.<hr><table border='1' cellpadding='3' cellspacing='0' width='100%'><tr bgcolor='#CCCCFF' class='TableHeadingColor'><td colspan='3'><font size='+2'><b>Client Events</b></font></td></tr><tr><td><b>Name</b></td><td><b>Description</b></td><td><b>Supported classes for argument</b></td><tr><tr><td>start</td><td>Fired when the target component starts to be dragged (default event). By default, no components are rendered in this ajax request, because rendering this draggable component itself or the target component could cause a dynamic update that replaces the original nodes being dragged on the page, which could interrupt the dragging action for the user.</td><td>javax.faces.event.AjaxBehaviorEvent</td></tr></table><i>Client events can be used with Client Behaviors and the ace:ajax tag.</i><br>]]></description>
<name>draggable</name>
<tag-class>org.icefaces.ace.component.dnd.DraggableTag</tag-class>
<body-content>JSP</body-content>
<attribute>
<description><![CDATA[Restrict the drag movement of this item to an axis. Default is null, possible values include: "x" & "y".]]></description>
<name>axis</name>
<required>no</required>
<rtexprvalue>true</rtexprvalue>
<type>java.lang.String</type>
</attribute>
<attribute>
<description><![CDATA[Using an EL expression, bind the component reference to a bean property, so that the component may be accessed in the bean.]]></description>
<name>binding</name>
<required>no</required>
<rtexprvalue>true</rtexprvalue>
<type>javax.el.ValueExpression</type>
</attribute>
<attribute>
<description><![CDATA[Id of the parent component whose boundaries should restrict the movement of this draggable.]]></description>
<name>containment</name>
<required>no</required>
<rtexprvalue>true</rtexprvalue>
<type>java.lang.String</type>
</attribute>
<attribute>
<description><![CDATA[Cursor style to set when this component is being dragged. See <a href="http://www.quirksmode.org/css/cursor.html">this page</a> for a reference of what cursor styles your browser supports.]]></description>
<name>cursor</name>
<required>no</required>
<rtexprvalue>true</rtexprvalue>
<type>java.lang.String</type>
</attribute>
<attribute>
<description><![CDATA[Allows you to set the ID of an UIData component that will provide a Java object as input for the drag start event. That object is defined by matching the index of the draggable to an object at the same index in the UIData component backing.]]></description>
<name>datasource</name>
<required>no</required>
<rtexprvalue>true</rtexprvalue>
<type>java.lang.String</type>
</attribute>
<attribute>
<description><![CDATA[If set, movement is disabled.]]></description>
<name>disabled</name>
<required>no</required>
<rtexprvalue>true</rtexprvalue>
<type>boolean</type>
</attribute>
<attribute>
<description><![CDATA[If set, component won't cause drop event.]]></description>
<name>dragOnly</name>
<required>no</required>
<rtexprvalue>true</rtexprvalue>
<type>boolean</type>
</attribute>
<attribute>
<description><![CDATA[MethodExpression reference to a method called whenever the target component starts to be dragged. (It is advised not to use this event for updating the component being dragged, in order to avoid having its markup replaced while still dragging it. See wiki for more details.)]]></description>
<name>dragStartListener</name>
<required>no</required>
<rtexprvalue>true</rtexprvalue>
<type>javax.el.MethodExpression</type>
</attribute>
<attribute>
<description><![CDATA[Id of the component to add draggable behavior to.]]></description>
<name>for</name>
<required>no</required>
<rtexprvalue>true</rtexprvalue>
<type>java.lang.String</type>
</attribute>
<attribute>
<description><![CDATA[Defines the drag movement of this component as though snapping to a grid in defined intervals. Ex: '20x20', measured in pixels.]]></description>
<name>grid</name>
<required>no</required>
<rtexprvalue>true</rtexprvalue>
<type>java.lang.String</type>
</attribute>
<attribute>
<description><![CDATA[Restrict the drag-event start to an element specified by this JQuery selector.]]></description>
<name>handle</name>
<required>no</required>
<rtexprvalue>true</rtexprvalue>
<type>java.lang.String</type>
</attribute>
<attribute>
<description><![CDATA[Specifies which element to move during the dragging event. Possible values are 'original' or 'clone'.]]></description>
<name>helper</name>
<required>no</required>
<rtexprvalue>true</rtexprvalue>
<type>java.lang.String</type>
</attribute>
<attribute>
<description><![CDATA[The component identifier for this component. This value must be unique within the closest parent component that is a naming container.]]></description>
<name>id</name>
<required>no</required>
<rtexprvalue>true</rtexprvalue>
<type>java.lang.String</type>
</attribute>
<attribute>
<description><![CDATA[The opacity for the helper during dragging. Values can range from 0.00 to 1.00. Default = '1.0'.]]></description>
<name>opacity</name>
<required>no</required>
<rtexprvalue>true</rtexprvalue>
<type>java.lang.Double</type>
</attribute>
<attribute>
<description><![CDATA[Return true if this component (and its children) should be rendered during the Render Response phase of the request processing lifecycle. Default = 'true'.]]></description>
<name>rendered</name>
<required>no</required>
<rtexprvalue>true</rtexprvalue>
<type>boolean</type>
</attribute>
<attribute>
<description><![CDATA[If set, the component will return to its original position when dragging stops.]]></description>
<name>revert</name>
<required>no</required>
<rtexprvalue>true</rtexprvalue>
<type>boolean</type>
</attribute>
<attribute>
<description><![CDATA[This arbitrary keyword allows sets of dragabbles and droppables with the same keyword to be associated with each other exclusively.]]></description>
<name>scope</name>
<required>no</required>
<rtexprvalue>true</rtexprvalue>
<type>java.lang.String</type>
</attribute>
<attribute>
<description><![CDATA[Enable 'snap to droppable' behavior for this component.]]></description>
<name>snap</name>
<required>no</required>
<rtexprvalue>true</rtexprvalue>
<type>boolean</type>
</attribute>
<attribute>
<description><![CDATA[Specifies which edges on elements to snap to. Possible values include: outer, inner and both.]]></description>
<name>snapMode</name>
<required>no</required>
<rtexprvalue>true</rtexprvalue>
<type>java.lang.String</type>
</attribute>
<attribute>
<description><![CDATA[Distance in pixels from the droppable edges at which snapping should occur.]]></description>
<name>snapTolerance</name>
<required>no</required>
<rtexprvalue>true</rtexprvalue>
<type>int</type>
</attribute>
<attribute>
<description><![CDATA[JQuery selector that defines the set of items this draggable shares its space with, ensures this item is brought to the front z-index when dragged.]]></description>
<name>stack</name>
<required>no</required>
<rtexprvalue>true</rtexprvalue>
<type>java.lang.String</type>
</attribute>
<attribute>
<description><![CDATA[The JavaScript component instance variable name.]]></description>
<name>widgetVar</name>
<required>no</required>
<rtexprvalue>true</rtexprvalue>
<type>java.lang.String</type>
</attribute>
<attribute>
<description><![CDATA[The z-index to set for the helper object.]]></description>
<name>zindex</name>
<required>no</required>
<rtexprvalue>true</rtexprvalue>
<type>int</type>
</attribute>
</tag>
<tag>
<description><![CDATA[Allows a specified component to act as an area where Draggable items can be moved onto and register the event.<p>For more information, see the <a href="http://wiki.icefaces.org/display/ICE/Droppable">Droppable Wiki Documentation</a>.<hr><table border='1' cellpadding='3' cellspacing='0' width='100%'><tr bgcolor='#CCCCFF' class='TableHeadingColor'><td colspan='3'><font size='+2'><b>Client Events</b></font></td></tr><tr><td><b>Name</b></td><td><b>Description</b></td><td><b>Supported classes for argument</b></td><tr><tr><td>drop</td><td>Fired when a draggable component is dropped on this droppable component (default event). By default, both the draggable and the droppable components are executed in this ajax request.</td><td>javax.faces.event.AjaxBehaviorEvent</td></tr></table><i>Client events can be used with Client Behaviors and the ace:ajax tag.</i><br>]]></description>
<name>droppable</name>
<tag-class>org.icefaces.ace.component.dnd.DroppableTag</tag-class>
<body-content>JSP</body-content>
<attribute>
<description><![CDATA[JQuery selector to define the set of acceptable draggables.]]></description>
<name>accept</name>
<required>no</required>
<rtexprvalue>true</rtexprvalue>
<type>java.lang.String</type>
</attribute>
<attribute>
<description><![CDATA[Class to apply to the droppable component when an acceptable draggable is dropped.]]></description>
<name>activeStyleClass</name>
<required>no</required>
<rtexprvalue>true</rtexprvalue>
<type>java.lang.String</type>
</attribute>
<attribute>
<description><![CDATA[Using an EL expression, bind the component reference to a bean property, so that the component may be accessed in the bean.]]></description>
<name>binding</name>
<required>no</required>
<rtexprvalue>true</rtexprvalue>
<type>javax.el.ValueExpression</type>
</attribute>
<attribute>
<description><![CDATA[Allows you to set the ID of an ACE UIData component and that will provide a Java object as input for the drop event. That object is defined by matching the sibling index of the droppable to an object at that index in the UIData component backing.]]></description>
<name>datasource</name>
<required>no</required>
<rtexprvalue>true</rtexprvalue>
<type>java.lang.String</type>
</attribute>
<attribute>
<description><![CDATA[If enabled, no draggables will activate this droppable.]]></description>
<name>disabled</name>
<required>no</required>
<rtexprvalue>true</rtexprvalue>
<type>boolean</type>
</attribute>
<attribute>
<description><![CDATA[MethodExpression reference to a method called whenever a draggable is moved into this droppable. The method receives a single argument, DragDropEvent.]]></description>
<name>dropListener</name>
<required>no</required>
<rtexprvalue>true</rtexprvalue>
<type>javax.el.MethodExpression</type>
</attribute>
<attribute>
<description><![CDATA[Id of the component to add the droppable behavior to.]]></description>
<name>for</name>
<required>no</required>
<rtexprvalue>true</rtexprvalue>
<type>java.lang.String</type>
</attribute>
<attribute>
<description><![CDATA[Class to apply to the droppable component when an acceptable draggable is hovering.]]></description>
<name>hoverStyleClass</name>
<required>no</required>
<rtexprvalue>true</rtexprvalue>
<type>java.lang.String</type>
</attribute>
<attribute>
<description><![CDATA[The component identifier for this component. This value must be unique within the closest parent component that is a naming container.]]></description>
<name>id</name>
<required>no</required>
<rtexprvalue>true</rtexprvalue>
<type>java.lang.String</type>
</attribute>
<attribute>
<description><![CDATA[Return true if this component (and its children) should be rendered during the Render Response phase of the request processing lifecycle. Default = 'true'.]]></description>
<name>rendered</name>
<required>no</required>
<rtexprvalue>true</rtexprvalue>
<type>boolean</type>
</attribute>
<attribute>
<description><![CDATA[This keyword allows sets of dragabbles and droppables with the same keyword to be associated with each other exclusively.]]></description>
<name>scope</name>
<required>no</required>
<rtexprvalue>true</rtexprvalue>
<type>java.lang.String</type>
</attribute>
<attribute>
<description><![CDATA[This arbitrary keyword specifies the method of checking if a draggable is 'over' the droppable, possible values include: fit (drag must be smaller), intersect (drag must cover > 50%). pointer (cursor must be inside drop) and touch (any of the drop touches).]]></description>
<name>tolerance</name>
<required>no</required>
<rtexprvalue>true</rtexprvalue>
<type>java.lang.String</type>
</attribute>
<attribute>
<description><![CDATA[The JavaScript component instance variable name.]]></description>
<name>widgetVar</name>
<required>no</required>
<rtexprvalue>true</rtexprvalue>
<type>java.lang.String</type>
</attribute>
</tag>
<tag>
<description><![CDATA[The DataView component renders a table region for iterative output using columns defined with the required DataViewColumns component child, and a detail region for extensive viewing (and editing) of the row objects of the table model. The detail regionis defined with the DataViewDetails child component and it's contents are displayed when a row of table region is activated, typically by a row tap.]]></description>
<name>dataView</name>
<tag-class>org.icefaces.ace.component.dataview.DataViewTag</tag-class>
<body-content>JSP</body-content>
<attribute>
<description><![CDATA[This enumeration defines the operation of the detail region. When set to 'server' (the default) the detail region may contain arbitrary JSF components and is rendered by an ajax request. When set to 'client' an activation 'renders' the detail region by updating, entirely on the client, an existing rendering with the dynamic attributes unique to an iterative rendering. The components and attributes supported for client encoding are limited, though growing with new releases and user desire.Specifics can be found on our wiki at: http://www.icesoft.org/wiki/display/icemobile/DataView Default = 'org.icefaces.ace.component.dataview.ActivationMode.server'.]]></description>
<name>activationMode</name>
<required>no</required>
<rtexprvalue>true</rtexprvalue>
<type>org.icefaces.ace.component.dataview.ActivationMode</type>
</attribute>
<attribute>
<description><![CDATA[ActiveRowIndex property allows control of the row object index currently displayed in the detail region. The detail region components instances are not updated until DataView.initDetailContext() is called. initDetailContext is regularly called within the component phase iterations.]]></description>
<name>activeRowIndex</name>
<required>no</required>
<rtexprvalue>true</rtexprvalue>
<type>java.lang.Integer</type>
</attribute>
<attribute>
<description><![CDATA[Using an EL expression, bind the component reference to a bean property, so that the component may be accessed in the bean.]]></description>
<name>binding</name>
<required>no</required>
<rtexprvalue>true</rtexprvalue>
<type>javax.el.ValueExpression</type>
</attribute>
<attribute>
<description><![CDATA[Disables this component, so it does not receive focus or get submitted.]]></description>
<name>disabled</name>
<required>no</required>
<rtexprvalue>true</rtexprvalue>
<type>boolean</type>
</attribute>
<attribute>
<description><![CDATA[The component identifier for this component. This value must be unique within the closest parent component that is a naming container.]]></description>
<name>id</name>
<required>no</required>
<rtexprvalue>true</rtexprvalue>
<type>java.lang.String</type>
</attribute>
<attribute>
<description><![CDATA[Enabling causes the table region to display as many columns as possible in the given device width, hiding the remainder, following priority given with the 'reactivePriority' attribute of DataViewColumnModel. Default = 'false'.]]></description>
<name>reactiveColumnVisibility</name>
<required>no</required>
<rtexprvalue>true</rtexprvalue>
<type>boolean</type>
</attribute>
<attribute>
<description><![CDATA[Return true if this component (and its children) should be rendered during the Render Response phase of the request processing lifecycle. Default = 'true'.]]></description>
<name>rendered</name>
<required>no</required>
<rtexprvalue>true</rtexprvalue>
<type>boolean</type>
</attribute>
<attribute>
<description><![CDATA[Define the Expression Language variable name to be given to the index of the row object during iterative rendering, either in the ValueExpressions of a DataViewColumnModel defining a table cell or within the components of the detail region.]]></description>
<name>rowIndexVar</name>
<required>no</required>
<rtexprvalue>true</rtexprvalue>
<type>java.lang.String</type>
</attribute>
<attribute>
<description><![CDATA[Renders cell background shading on the odd numbered rows.]]></description>
<name>rowStripe</name>
<required>no</required>
<rtexprvalue>true</rtexprvalue>
<type>boolean</type>
</attribute>
<attribute>
<description><![CDATA[Renders faint bottom border to each row. Default = 'true'.]]></description>
<name>rowStroke</name>
<required>no</required>
<rtexprvalue>true</rtexprvalue>
<type>boolean</type>
</attribute>
<attribute>
<description><![CDATA[Sets the CSS style definition to be applied to this component.]]></description>
<name>style</name>
<required>no</required>
<rtexprvalue>true</rtexprvalue>
<type>java.lang.String</type>
</attribute>
<attribute>
<description><![CDATA[Sets the CSS class to apply to this component.]]></description>
<name>styleClass</name>
<required>no</required>
<rtexprvalue>true</rtexprvalue>
<type>java.lang.String</type>
</attribute>
<attribute>
<description><![CDATA[Define the index-based data model of DataView, currently supported types include List and instances of DataViewLazyDataModel.]]></description>
<name>value</name>
<required>no</required>
<rtexprvalue>true</rtexprvalue>
<type>java.lang.Object</type>
</attribute>
<attribute>
<description><![CDATA[Define the Expression Language variable name to be given to the row object during iterative rendering, either in the ValueExpressions of a DataViewColumnModel defining a table cell or within the components of the detail region.]]></description>
<name>var</name>
<required>no</required>
<rtexprvalue>true</rtexprvalue>
<type>java.lang.String</type>
</attribute>
</tag>
<tag>
<description><![CDATA[The DataViewColumns component defines the table region of the DataView component either by its DataViewColumn child components or by attaching an implementationof DataViewColumnsModel to the 'value' attribute of this component.]]></description>
<name>dataViewColumns</name>
<tag-class>org.icefaces.ace.component.dataview.DataViewColumnsTag</tag-class>
<body-content>JSP</body-content>
<attribute>
<description><![CDATA[Define the table model of the DataView component programatically with an implementation of DataViewColumnsModel.]]></description>
<name>value</name>
<required>no</required>
<rtexprvalue>true</rtexprvalue>
<type>java.lang.Object</type>
</attribute>
</tag>
<tag>
<description><![CDATA[DataViewColumns defines a column in the table region of the DataView component.]]></description>
<name>dataViewColumn</name>
<tag-class>org.icefaces.ace.component.dataview.DataViewColumnTag</tag-class>
<body-content>JSP</body-content>
<attribute>
<description><![CDATA[Define the text to render in the footer of this column.]]></description>
<name>footerText</name>
<required>no</required>
<rtexprvalue>true</rtexprvalue>
<type>java.lang.String</type>
</attribute>
<attribute>
<description><![CDATA[Define the text to render in the header of this column.]]></description>
<name>headerText</name>
<required>no</required>
<rtexprvalue>true</rtexprvalue>
<type>java.lang.String</type>
</attribute>
<attribute>
<description><![CDATA[Define a String of arbitrary HTML markup to render (when 'type' is set to 'markup') replacing the substring {{value}} with the String representation of the 'value' attribute.]]></description>
<name>markup</name>
<required>no</required>
<rtexprvalue>true</rtexprvalue>
<type>java.lang.String</type>
</attribute>
<attribute>
<description><![CDATA[Define the order that columns are displayed when hiding columns in width constrained cases. Property has no effect unless the 'reactiveColumnVisibility' property of the DataView is enabled. If priority for a given column is unset, priority is assigned in the same order as page markup, following the column with the highest explicit priority.]]></description>
<name>reactivePriority</name>
<required>no</required>
<rtexprvalue>true</rtexprvalue>
<type>java.lang.Integer</type>
</attribute>
<attribute>
<description><![CDATA[Sets the CSS class to apply to this component.]]></description>
<name>styleClass</name>
<required>no</required>
<rtexprvalue>true</rtexprvalue>
<type>java.lang.String</type>
</attribute>
<attribute>
<description><![CDATA[Define the ColumnType of this column, determining how the 'value' attribute of this component will be rendered. Valid options include : text, bool, date, image, markup.
Text will render the String representation of the value object.
Bool assumes the value object is a boolean type and renders a checkbox icon.
Date assumes the value object is a Date object and renders according to the required f:dateTimeConverter child component.
Image assume the value is a representation of an image URL.
Markup renders the String 'markup' attribute with the substring '{{value}}' replaced with the String representation of the value object. Default = 'org.icefaces.ace.component.dataview.ColumnType.text'.]]></description>
<name>type</name>
<required>no</required>
<rtexprvalue>true</rtexprvalue>
<type>org.icefaces.ace.component.dataview.ColumnType</type>
</attribute>
<attribute>
<description><![CDATA[Define a ValueExpression whose resulting Object will be iteratively rendered in the table region of the DataView according to the 'type' of this column.]]></description>
<name>value</name>
<required>no</required>
<rtexprvalue>true</rtexprvalue>
<type>java.lang.Object</type>
</attribute>
</tag>
<tag>
<description><![CDATA[The child components of this component define the region to be displayed when a row object of DataView table region is activated. When DataView 'activationMode' is set to 'server' the child components of this region may be arbitrary JSF components. When 'activationMode' is set to 'client' the child components of this region are prerendered and have their dynamic attributes cached on the client to allow instanteous activation. Client activation mode is restricted to particular components and only particular attributes of these components may be dynamic, the specifics are documented on our wiki.]]></description>
<name>dataViewDetails</name>
<tag-class>org.icefaces.ace.component.dataview.DataViewDetailsTag</tag-class>
<body-content>JSP</body-content>
</tag>
<tag>
<description><![CDATA[BreadcrumbMenu is a horizontal bar of breadcrumb menu items. The crumbs are encoded by child menuItem tags. The menu items can be encoded inline or dynamically using a menu model (org.icefaces.ace.model.MenuModel). The icon attribute is not used. The icon will be forced to a home page icon for the first item and a right arrow icon for the rest. The last (or only) item will also be forced to be disabled.]]></description>
<name>breadcrumbMenu</name>
<tag-class>org.icefaces.ace.component.breadcrumbmenu.BreadcrumbMenuTag</tag-class>
<body-content>JSP</body-content>
<attribute>
<description><![CDATA[Using an EL expression, bind the component reference to a bean property, so that the component may be accessed in the bean.]]></description>
<name>binding</name>
<required>no</required>
<rtexprvalue>true</rtexprvalue>
<type>javax.el.ValueExpression</type>
</attribute>
<attribute>
<description><![CDATA[The component identifier for this component. This value must be unique within the closest parent component that is a naming container.]]></description>
<name>id</name>
<required>no</required>
<rtexprvalue>true</rtexprvalue>
<type>java.lang.String</type>
</attribute>
<attribute>
<description><![CDATA[MenuModel instance to create menus programmatically. For the menuitem components, use explicit ids, and avoid long processing in the getter method for this property, as it will be called multiple times, in every lifecycle.]]></description>
<name>model</name>
<required>no</required>
<rtexprvalue>true</rtexprvalue>
<type>org.icefaces.ace.model.MenuModel</type>
</attribute>
<attribute>
<description><![CDATA[Return true if this component (and its children) should be rendered during the Render Response phase of the request processing lifecycle. Default = 'true'.]]></description>
<name>rendered</name>
<required>no</required>
<rtexprvalue>true</rtexprvalue>
<type>boolean</type>
</attribute>
<attribute>
<description><![CDATA[Style of the main container element.]]></description>
<name>style</name>
<required>no</required>
<rtexprvalue>true</rtexprvalue>
<type>java.lang.String</type>
</attribute>
<attribute>
<description><![CDATA[Style class of the main container element.]]></description>
<name>styleClass</name>
<required>no</required>
<rtexprvalue>true</rtexprvalue>
<type>java.lang.String</type>
</attribute>
</tag>
<tag>
<description><![CDATA[Display Faces messages in a Growl container positioned on one of the four corners of the browser window.]]></description>
<name>growlMessages</name>
<tag-class>org.icefaces.ace.component.growlmessages.GrowlMessagesTag</tag-class>
<body-content>JSP</body-content>
<attribute>
<description><![CDATA[Types of messages to auto hide after display: "true" (auto hide all messages), "false" (don't auto hide any message), "info", "warn", "error", or "fatal" (auto hide messages at or below specified severity.) Default = 'true'.]]></description>
<name>autoHide</name>
<required>no</required>
<rtexprvalue>true</rtexprvalue>
<type>java.lang.String</type>
</attribute>
<attribute>
<description><![CDATA[Using an EL expression, bind the component reference to a bean property, so that the component may be accessed in the bean.]]></description>
<name>binding</name>
<required>no</required>
<rtexprvalue>true</rtexprvalue>
<type>javax.el.ValueExpression</type>
</attribute>
<attribute>
<description><![CDATA[Whether or not the close-all button should be used when more than one notification appears on the screen. (Close visible messages only, not hidden messages.) Default = 'true'.]]></description>
<name>closeAll</name>
<required>no</required>
<rtexprvalue>true</rtexprvalue>
<type>boolean</type>
</attribute>
<attribute>
<description><![CDATA[The lifespan (milliseconds) of an auto-hide message on the screen. Default = '3000'.]]></description>
<name>displayDuration</name>
<required>no</required>
<rtexprvalue>true</rtexprvalue>
<type>int</type>
</attribute>
<attribute>
<description><![CDATA[Flag indicating that characters that are sensitive in HTML and XML markup must be escaped. Note: setting this to false may open up security issues. See <a href="https://www.owasp.org/index.php/XSS_(Cross_Site_Scripting)_Prevention_Cheat_Sheet">XSS (Cross Site Scripting) Prevention Cheat Sheet.</a> Default = 'true'.]]></description>
<name>escape</name>
<required>no</required>
<rtexprvalue>true</rtexprvalue>
<type>boolean</type>
</attribute>
<attribute>
<description><![CDATA[Identifier of the component for which to render error messages. If this component is within the same NamingContainer as the target component, this must be the component identifier. Otherwise, it must be an absolute component identifier (starting with ":"). Leave out or use "@all" to output global messages.]]></description>
<name>for</name>
<required>no</required>
<rtexprvalue>true</rtexprvalue>
<type>java.lang.String</type>
</attribute>
<attribute>
<description><![CDATA[Flag indicating whether only global messages (that is, messages with no associated client identifier) should be rendered. Mutually exclusive with the 'for' property which takes precedence. Default = 'false'.]]></description>
<name>globalOnly</name>
<required>no</required>
<rtexprvalue>true</rtexprvalue>
<type>boolean</type>
</attribute>
<attribute>
<description><![CDATA[Header to prefix a message. Default = ''.]]></description>
<name>header</name>
<required>no</required>
<rtexprvalue>true</rtexprvalue>
<type>java.lang.String</type>
</attribute>
<attribute>
<description><![CDATA[Duration (also called "speed" in jQuery) of hide effect. Values and default same as for showEffectDuration. Default = '_default'.]]></description>
<name>hideEffectDuration</name>
<required>no</required>
<rtexprvalue>true</rtexprvalue>
<type>java.lang.String</type>
</attribute>
<attribute>
<description><![CDATA[The component identifier for this component. This value must be unique within the closest parent component that is a naming container.]]></description>
<name>id</name>
<required>no</required>
<rtexprvalue>true</rtexprvalue>
<type>java.lang.String</type>
</attribute>
<attribute>
<description><![CDATA[Limit the number of messages appearing at a given time to this number. Default is 0, no limit. Default = '0'.]]></description>
<name>maxVisibleMessages</name>
<required>no</required>
<rtexprvalue>true</rtexprvalue>
<type>int</type>
</attribute>
<attribute>
<description><![CDATA[Designates whether a notification should be appended to the container after all notifications, or whether it should be prepended to the container before all notifications. Options are "after" or "before". Default = 'after'.]]></description>
<name>messageOrder</name>
<required>no</required>
<rtexprvalue>true</rtexprvalue>
<type>java.lang.String</type>
</attribute>
<attribute>
<description><![CDATA[A CSS class to be applied to each notification when they are created. Default = ''.]]></description>
<name>messageStyleClass</name>
<required>no</required>
<rtexprvalue>true</rtexprvalue>
<type>java.lang.String</type>
</attribute>
<attribute>
<description><![CDATA[Designates a class which is applied to the growl container and controls its position on the screen. Options: top-left, top-right, bottom-left, bottom-right. Default = 'top-right'.]]></description>
<name>position</name>
<required>no</required>
<rtexprvalue>true</rtexprvalue>
<type>java.lang.String</type>
</attribute>
<attribute>
<description><![CDATA[A flag indicating this UIMessages instance should redisplay FacesMessages that have already been handled. Default = 'true'.]]></description>
<name>redisplay</name>
<required>no</required>
<rtexprvalue>true</rtexprvalue>
<type>boolean</type>
</attribute>
<attribute>
<description><![CDATA[Return true if this component (and its children) should be rendered during the Render Response phase of the request processing lifecycle. Default = 'true'.]]></description>
<name>rendered</name>
<required>no</required>
<rtexprvalue>true</rtexprvalue>
<type>boolean</type>
</attribute>
<attribute>
<description><![CDATA[Flag indicating whether the "detail" property of messages for the specified component should be rendered. Default = 'false'.]]></description>
<name>showDetail</name>
<required>no</required>
<rtexprvalue>true</rtexprvalue>
<type>boolean</type>
</attribute>
<attribute>
<description><![CDATA[Duration (also called "speed" in jQuery) of show effect. One of "slow", "_default", "fast", or an integer of milliseconds. ("slow", "_default", "fast" currently equated to 600, 400 and 200 respectively in jQuery.) Default = '_default'.]]></description>
<name>showEffectDuration</name>
<required>no</required>
<rtexprvalue>true</rtexprvalue>
<type>java.lang.String</type>
</attribute>
<attribute>
<description><![CDATA[Flag indicating whether the "summary" property of messages for the specified component should be rendered. Default = 'true'.]]></description>
<name>showSummary</name>
<required>no</required>
<rtexprvalue>true</rtexprvalue>
<type>boolean</type>
</attribute>
</tag>
<tag>
<description><![CDATA[<p>Renders a set of controls that reveal, submit and hide the hidden input facet of a  ace:cellEditor.</p><p>For more information, see the <a href="http://wiki.icefaces.org/display/ICE/RowEditor">Row Editor Wiki Documentation</a>.</p>]]></description>
<name>rowEditor</name>
<tag-class>org.icefaces.ace.component.roweditor.RowEditorTag</tag-class>
<body-content>JSP</body-content>
<attribute>
<description><![CDATA[Using an EL expression, bind the component reference to a bean property, so that the component may be accessed in the bean.]]></description>
<name>binding</name>
<required>no</required>
<rtexprvalue>true</rtexprvalue>
<type>javax.el.ValueExpression</type>
</attribute>
<attribute>
<description><![CDATA[Define a String title attribute for the cancel editing button. This will be shown as a browser tooltip when hovering over the icon. The default for this tooltip is definedin the ace messages bundle for easy i18n.]]></description>
<name>cancelTitle</name>
<required>no</required>
<rtexprvalue>true</rtexprvalue>
<type>java.lang.String</type>
</attribute>
<attribute>
<description><![CDATA[The component identifier for this component. This value must be unique within the closest parent component that is a naming container.]]></description>
<name>id</name>
<required>no</required>
<rtexprvalue>true</rtexprvalue>
<type>java.lang.String</type>
</attribute>
<attribute>
<description><![CDATA[Return true if this component (and its children) should be rendered during the Render Response phase of the request processing lifecycle. Default = 'true'.]]></description>
<name>rendered</name>
<required>no</required>
<rtexprvalue>true</rtexprvalue>
<type>boolean</type>
</attribute>
<attribute>
<description><![CDATA[MethodExpression reference called whenever a table row editing is canceled. The method receives a single argument, RowEditCancelEvent.]]></description>
<name>rowEditCancelListener</name>
<required>no</required>
<rtexprvalue>true</rtexprvalue>
<type>javax.el.MethodExpression</type>
</attribute>
<attribute>
<description><![CDATA[MethodExpression reference called whenever a table row is edited. The method receives a single argument, RowEditEvent.]]></description>
<name>rowEditListener</name>
<required>no</required>
<rtexprvalue>true</rtexprvalue>
<type>javax.el.MethodExpression</type>
</attribute>
<attribute>
<description><![CDATA[Define a String title attribute for the begin editing button. This will be shown as a browser tooltip when hovering over the icon. The default for this tooltip is definedin the ace messages bundle for easy i18n.]]></description>
<name>startTitle</name>
<required>no</required>
<rtexprvalue>true</rtexprvalue>
<type>java.lang.String</type>
</attribute>
<attribute>
<description><![CDATA[Define a String title attribute for the finish editing row button. This will be shown as a browser tooltip when hovering over the icon. The default for this tooltip is definedin the ace messages bundle for easy i18n.]]></description>
<name>submitTitle</name>
<required>no</required>
<rtexprvalue>true</rtexprvalue>
<type>java.lang.String</type>
</attribute>
</tag>
<tag>
<description><![CDATA[Printer allows sending a specific JSF component to the printer, not the whole page. It needs to be nested inside an h:commandButton or h:outputLink component.<p>For more information, see the <a href="http://wiki.icefaces.org/display/ICE/Printer">Printer Wiki Documentation</a>.<hr><table border='1' cellpadding='3' cellspacing='0' width='100%'><tr bgcolor='#CCCCFF' class='TableHeadingColor'><td colspan='3'><font size='+2'><b>Client Events</b></font></td></tr><tr><td><b>Name</b></td><td><b>Description</b></td><td><b>Supported classes for argument</b></td><tr><tr><td>activate</td><td>Fired when the parent component is clicked or activated via the keyboard (default event).</td><td>javax.faces.event.AjaxBehaviorEvent</td></tr></table><i>Client events can be used with Client Behaviors and the ace:ajax tag.</i><br>]]></description>
<name>printer</name>
<tag-class>org.icefaces.ace.component.printer.PrinterTag</tag-class>
<body-content>JSP</body-content>
<attribute>
<description><![CDATA[Using an EL expression, bind the component reference to a bean property, so that the component may be accessed in the bean.]]></description>
<name>binding</name>
<required>no</required>
<rtexprvalue>true</rtexprvalue>
<type>javax.el.ValueExpression</type>
</attribute>
<attribute>
<description><![CDATA[Specifies the id of the component to print.]]></description>
<name>for</name>
<required>no</required>
<rtexprvalue>true</rtexprvalue>
<type>java.lang.String</type>
</attribute>
<attribute>
<description><![CDATA[The component identifier for this component. This value must be unique within the closest parent component that is a naming container.]]></description>
<name>id</name>
<required>no</required>
<rtexprvalue>true</rtexprvalue>
<type>java.lang.String</type>
</attribute>
<attribute>
<description><![CDATA[If an ajax behavior is attached to this component, the print interface will appear whether validation failed or not for the ajax request fi this attribute is set to true. Otherwise, the printing action will be halted. Default = 'true'.]]></description>
<name>ignoreValidation</name>
<required>no</required>
<rtexprvalue>true</rtexprvalue>
<type>boolean</type>
</attribute>
<attribute>
<description><![CDATA[Return true if this component (and its children) should be rendered during the Render Response phase of the request processing lifecycle. Default = 'true'.]]></description>
<name>rendered</name>
<required>no</required>
<rtexprvalue>true</rtexprvalue>
<type>boolean</type>
</attribute>
</tag>
<tag>
<description><![CDATA[outputListItems is used within an outputList tag to group lists of items.]]></description>
<name>outputListItems</name>
<tag-class>org.icefaces.ace.component.outputlist.OutputListItemsTag</tag-class>
<body-content>JSP</body-content>
<attribute>
<description><![CDATA[Using an EL expression, bind the component reference to a bean property, so that the component may be accessed in the bean.]]></description>
<name>binding</name>
<required>no</required>
<rtexprvalue>true</rtexprvalue>
<type>javax.el.ValueExpression</type>
</attribute>
<attribute>
<description><![CDATA[Zero-relative row number of the first row in the underlying data model to be displayed, or zero to start at the beginning of the data model. Default = '0'.]]></description>
<name>first</name>
<required>no</required>
<rtexprvalue>true</rtexprvalue>
<type>int</type>
</attribute>
<attribute>
<description><![CDATA[The component identifier for this component. This value must be unique within the closest parent component that is a naming container.]]></description>
<name>id</name>
<required>no</required>
<rtexprvalue>true</rtexprvalue>
<type>java.lang.String</type>
</attribute>
<attribute>
<description><![CDATA[Determines if inset padding is included around list group. Default = 'false'.]]></description>
<name>inset</name>
<required>no</required>
<rtexprvalue>true</rtexprvalue>
<type>boolean</type>
</attribute>
<attribute>
<description><![CDATA[Return true if this component (and its children) should be rendered during the Render Response phase of the request processing lifecycle. Default = 'true'.]]></description>
<name>rendered</name>
<required>no</required>
<rtexprvalue>true</rtexprvalue>
<type>boolean</type>
</attribute>
<attribute>
<description><![CDATA[Zero-relative index of the row currently being accessed in the underlying DataModel, or -1 for no current row. Default = '0'.]]></description>
<name>rowIndex</name>
<required>no</required>
<rtexprvalue>true</rtexprvalue>
<type>int</type>
</attribute>
<attribute>
<description><![CDATA[The number of rows (starting with the one identified by the first property) to be displayed, or zero to display the entire set of available rows. Default = '0'.]]></description>
<name>rows</name>
<required>no</required>
<rtexprvalue>true</rtexprvalue>
<type>int</type>
</attribute>
<attribute>
<description><![CDATA[Sets the CSS style definition to be applied to this component.]]></description>
<name>style</name>
<required>no</required>
<rtexprvalue>true</rtexprvalue>
<type>java.lang.String</type>
</attribute>
<attribute>
<description><![CDATA[Sets the CSS class to apply to this component.]]></description>
<name>styleClass</name>
<required>no</required>
<rtexprvalue>true</rtexprvalue>
<type>java.lang.String</type>
</attribute>
<attribute>
<description><![CDATA[The DataModel instance representing the data to which this component is bound, or a collection of data for which a DataModel instance is synthesized.]]></description>
<name>value</name>
<required>no</required>
<rtexprvalue>true</rtexprvalue>
<type>java.lang.Object</type>
</attribute>
<attribute>
<description><![CDATA[The request-scope attribute (if any) under which the data object for the current row will be exposed when iterating.]]></description>
<name>var</name>
<required>no</required>
<rtexprvalue>true</rtexprvalue>
<type>java.lang.String</type>
</attribute>
<attribute>
<description><![CDATA[Name of a request-scope attribute under which the current indexed state will be exposed. This is modeled after the Facelets JSTL c:forEach varStatus, and has 5 sub-properties:</p><dl><dt>int <b>begin</b></dt> <dd>Corresponds to the UIData container's <b>first</b> property, the     index at which it begins iteration.</dd><dt>int <b>end</b></dt><dd>The ending index of iteration, corresponding to the UIData     container's <b>first</b> plus <b>rows</b> minus 1. Note:     If the UIData's DataModel's isRowAvailable() method returns false,     prematurely ending iteration, then the actual ending index may not     equal the value for this <b>end</b> property.</dd><dt>int <b>index</b></dt><dd>The current iteration index. Corresponding to the UIData     container's getRowIndex() value, which also corresponds with the     UIData's DataModel's getRowIndex() value.</dd><dt>boolean <b>first</b></dt><dd>Defined simply as: <b>varStatus.index == varStatus.begin</b></dd><dt>boolean <b>last</b></dt><dd>Defined simply as: <b>varStatus.index == varStatus.end</b>. Note:     This has the same limitations as the <b>end</b> property.</dd>]]></description>
<name>varStatus</name>
<required>no</required>
<rtexprvalue>true</rtexprvalue>
<type>java.lang.String</type>
</attribute>
</tag>
<tag>
<description><![CDATA[outputList defines a grouping of unordered list items.  The child component of this component must be outputListItem components. ]]></description>
