<tag>
<description><![CDATA[MaskedEntry is an input component that forces text input to be entered according to a specified format.<p>For more information, see the <a href="http://wiki.icefaces.org/display/ICE/MaskedEntry">MaskedEntry Wiki Documentation</a>.<hr><table border='1' cellpadding='3' cellspacing='0' width='100%'><tr bgcolor='#CCCCFF' class='TableHeadingColor'><td colspan='3'><font size='+2'><b>Client Events</b></font></td></tr><tr><td><b>Name</b></td><td><b>Description</b></td><td><b>Supported classes for argument</b></td><tr><tr><td>valueChange</td><td>Fired every time the value of the text input changes (default event). When pressing the ENTER key on the text field, this event will be fired as well, even if the value didn't actually change.</td><td>javax.faces.event.AjaxBehaviorEvent</td></tr><tr><td>keypress</td><td>Fired on a keypress event. Use only to read input char. Don't re-render or do JS-like event handling. Otherwise could cause focus and DOM update problems, losing both focus and value.</td><td>org.icefaces.ace.event.KeyPressEvent</td></tr><tr><td>blur</td><td>Fired any time the text input field loses focus.</td><td>javax.faces.event.AjaxBehaviorEvent</td></tr></table><i>Client events can be used with Client Behaviors and the ace:ajax tag.</i><br>]]></description>
<name>maskedEntry</name>
<tag-class>org.icefaces.ace.component.maskedentry.MaskedEntryTag</tag-class>
<body-content>JSP</body-content>
<attribute>
<description><![CDATA[Access key that, when pressed, transfers focus to this element.]]></description>
<name>accesskey</name>
<required>no</required>
<rtexprvalue>true</rtexprvalue>
<type>java.lang.String</type>
</attribute>
<attribute>
<description><![CDATA[Alternate textual description of the element rendered by this component.]]></description>
<name>alt</name>
<required>no</required>
<rtexprvalue>true</rtexprvalue>
<type>java.lang.String</type>
</attribute>
<attribute>
<description><![CDATA[If the value of this attribute is "off", render "off" as the value of the attribute. This indicates that the browser should disable its autocomplete feature for this component. This is useful for components that perform autocompletion and do not want the browser interfering. If this attribute is not set or the value is "on", render nothing.]]></description>
<name>autocomplete</name>
<required>no</required>
<rtexprvalue>true</rtexprvalue>
<type>java.lang.String</type>
</attribute>
<attribute>
<description><![CDATA[Using an EL expression, bind the component reference to a bean property, so that the component may be accessed in the bean.]]></description>
<name>binding</name>
<required>no</required>
<rtexprvalue>true</rtexprvalue>
<type>javax.el.ValueExpression</type>
</attribute>
<attribute>
<description><![CDATA[Converter is an interface describing a Java class that can perform Object-to-String and String-to-Object conversions between model data objects and a String representation of those objects that is suitable for rendering.]]></description>
<name>converter</name>
<required>no</required>
<rtexprvalue>true</rtexprvalue>
<type>javax.faces.convert.Converter</type>
</attribute>
<attribute>
<description><![CDATA[If present, will be used as the text of the converter message, replacing any message that comes from the converter.]]></description>
<name>converterMessage</name>
<required>no</required>
<rtexprvalue>true</rtexprvalue>
<type>java.lang.String</type>
</attribute>
<attribute>
<description><![CDATA[Direction indication for text that does not inherit directionality. Valid values are "LTR" (left-to-right) and "RTL" (right-to-left).]]></description>
<name>dir</name>
<required>no</required>
<rtexprvalue>true</rtexprvalue>
<type>java.lang.String</type>
</attribute>
<attribute>
<description><![CDATA[Flag indicating that this element must never receive focus or be included in a subsequent submit. A value of false causes no attribute to be rendered, while a value of true causes the attribute to be rendered as disabled="disabled". Default = 'false'.]]></description>
<name>disabled</name>
<required>no</required>
<rtexprvalue>true</rtexprvalue>
<type>boolean</type>
</attribute>
<attribute>
<description><![CDATA[The component identifier for this component. This value must be unique within the closest parent component that is a naming container.]]></description>
<name>id</name>
<required>no</required>
<rtexprvalue>true</rtexprvalue>
<type>java.lang.String</type>
</attribute>
<attribute>
<description><![CDATA[A flag indicating that conversion and validation of this component's value should occur during Apply Request Values phase instead of Process Validations phase. Default = 'false'.]]></description>
<name>immediate</name>
<required>no</required>
<rtexprvalue>true</rtexprvalue>
<type>boolean</type>
</attribute>
<attribute>
<description><![CDATA[Position of input-required or input-optional indicator relative to input field or label. Supported values are "left/right/top/bottom/labelLeft/labelRight/none". Default is "labelRight" if labelPosition is "inField", "right" otherwise.]]></description>
<name>indicatorPosition</name>
<required>no</required>
<rtexprvalue>true</rtexprvalue>
<type>java.lang.String</type>
</attribute>
<attribute>
<description><![CDATA[A localized user presentable name for this component.]]></description>
<name>label</name>
<required>no</required>
<rtexprvalue>true</rtexprvalue>
<type>java.lang.String</type>
</attribute>
<attribute>
<description><![CDATA[Position of label relative to input field. Supported values are "left/right/top/bottom/inField/none". Default is "none".]]></description>
<name>labelPosition</name>
<required>no</required>
<rtexprvalue>true</rtexprvalue>
<type>java.lang.String</type>
</attribute>
<attribute>
<description><![CDATA[Code describing the language used in the generated markup for this component.]]></description>
<name>lang</name>
<required>no</required>
<rtexprvalue>true</rtexprvalue>
<type>java.lang.String</type>
</attribute>
<attribute>
<description><![CDATA[Masked input for separating input texts with given pattern. 
These mask definitions can be used: 
a - Represents an alpha character (A-Z,a-z) 
9 - Represents a numeric character (0-9) 
* - Represents an alphanumeric character (A-Z,a-z,0-9). All input is optional. Any character not in the definitions list will be automatically entered for the user as they type.]]></description>
<name>mask</name>
<required>yes</required>
<rtexprvalue>true</rtexprvalue>
<type>java.lang.String</type>
</attribute>
<attribute>
<description><![CDATA[The maximum number of characters that may be entered in this field.]]></description>
<name>maxlength</name>
<required>no</required>
<rtexprvalue>true</rtexprvalue>
<type>int</type>
</attribute>
<attribute>
<description><![CDATA[Javascript code executed when this element loses focus.]]></description>
<name>onblur</name>
<required>no</required>
<rtexprvalue>true</rtexprvalue>
<type>java.lang.String</type>
</attribute>
<attribute>
<description><![CDATA[Javascript code executed when this element loses focus and its value has been modified since gaining focus.]]></description>
<name>onchange</name>
<required>no</required>
<rtexprvalue>true</rtexprvalue>
<type>java.lang.String</type>
</attribute>
<attribute>
<description><![CDATA[Javascript code executed when a pointer button is clicked over this element.]]></description>
<name>onclick</name>
<required>no</required>
<rtexprvalue>true</rtexprvalue>
<type>java.lang.String</type>
</attribute>
<attribute>
<description><![CDATA[Javascript code executed when a pointer button is double clicked over this element.]]></description>
<name>ondblclick</name>
<required>no</required>
<rtexprvalue>true</rtexprvalue>
<type>java.lang.String</type>
</attribute>
<attribute>
<description><![CDATA[Javascript code executed when this element receives focus.]]></description>
<name>onfocus</name>
<required>no</required>
<rtexprvalue>true</rtexprvalue>
<type>java.lang.String</type>
</attribute>
<attribute>
<description><![CDATA[Javascript code executed when a key is pressed down over this element.]]></description>
<name>onkeydown</name>
<required>no</required>
<rtexprvalue>true</rtexprvalue>
<type>java.lang.String</type>
</attribute>
<attribute>
<description><![CDATA[Javascript code executed when a key is pressed and released over this element.]]></description>
<name>onkeypress</name>
<required>no</required>
<rtexprvalue>true</rtexprvalue>
<type>java.lang.String</type>
</attribute>
<attribute>
<description><![CDATA[Javascript code executed when a key is released over this element.]]></description>
<name>onkeyup</name>
<required>no</required>
<rtexprvalue>true</rtexprvalue>
<type>java.lang.String</type>
</attribute>
<attribute>
<description><![CDATA[Javascript code executed when a pointer button is pressed down over this element.]]></description>
<name>onmousedown</name>
<required>no</required>
<rtexprvalue>true</rtexprvalue>
<type>java.lang.String</type>
</attribute>
<attribute>
<description><![CDATA[Javascript code executed when a pointer button is moved within this element.]]></description>
<name>onmousemove</name>
<required>no</required>
<rtexprvalue>true</rtexprvalue>
<type>java.lang.String</type>
</attribute>
<attribute>
<description><![CDATA[Javascript code executed when a pointer button is moved away from this element.]]></description>
<name>onmouseout</name>
<required>no</required>
<rtexprvalue>true</rtexprvalue>
<type>java.lang.String</type>
</attribute>
<attribute>
<description><![CDATA[Javascript code executed when a pointer button is moved onto this element.]]></description>
<name>onmouseover</name>
<required>no</required>
<rtexprvalue>true</rtexprvalue>
<type>java.lang.String</type>
</attribute>
<attribute>
<description><![CDATA[Javascript code executed when a pointer button is released over this element.]]></description>
<name>onmouseup</name>
<required>no</required>
<rtexprvalue>true</rtexprvalue>
<type>java.lang.String</type>
</attribute>
<attribute>
<description><![CDATA[Javascript code executed when text within this element is selected by the user.]]></description>
<name>onselect</name>
<required>no</required>
<rtexprvalue>true</rtexprvalue>
<type>java.lang.String</type>
</attribute>
<attribute>
<description><![CDATA[Indicator indicating that the user is NOT required to provide a submitted value for this input component.]]></description>
<name>optionalIndicator</name>
<required>no</required>
<rtexprvalue>true</rtexprvalue>
<type>java.lang.String</type>
</attribute>
<attribute>
<description><![CDATA[Separator and placeholder in input.]]></description>
<name>placeHolder</name>
<required>no</required>
<rtexprvalue>true</rtexprvalue>
<type>java.lang.String</type>
</attribute>
<attribute>
<description><![CDATA[Flag indicating that this component will prohibit changes by the user. The element may receive focus unless it has also been disabled. A value of false causes no attribute to be rendered, while a value of true causes the attribute to be rendered as readonly="readonly". Default = 'false'.]]></description>
<name>readonly</name>
<required>no</required>
<rtexprvalue>true</rtexprvalue>
<type>boolean</type>
</attribute>
<attribute>
<description><![CDATA[Return true if this component (and its children) should be rendered during the Render Response phase of the request processing lifecycle. Default = 'true'.]]></description>
<name>rendered</name>
<required>no</required>
<rtexprvalue>true</rtexprvalue>
<type>boolean</type>
</attribute>
<attribute>
<description><![CDATA[A flag indicating whether the user required to provide a non-empty submitted value for this component. Default = 'false'.]]></description>
<name>required</name>
<required>no</required>
<rtexprvalue>true</rtexprvalue>
<type>boolean</type>
</attribute>
<attribute>
<description><![CDATA[Indicator indicating that the user is required to provide a submitted value for this input component.]]></description>
<name>requiredIndicator</name>
<required>no</required>
<rtexprvalue>true</rtexprvalue>
<type>java.lang.String</type>
</attribute>
<attribute>
<description><![CDATA[If present, will be used as the text of the validation message for the "required" facility, if the "required" facility is used.]]></description>
<name>requiredMessage</name>
<required>no</required>
<rtexprvalue>true</rtexprvalue>
<type>java.lang.String</type>
</attribute>
<attribute>
<description><![CDATA[The number of characters used to determine the width of this field.]]></description>
<name>size</name>
<required>no</required>
<rtexprvalue>true</rtexprvalue>
<type>int</type>
</attribute>
<attribute>
<description><![CDATA[CSS style(s) to be applied when this component is rendered.]]></description>
<name>style</name>
<required>no</required>
<rtexprvalue>true</rtexprvalue>
<type>java.lang.String</type>
</attribute>
<attribute>
<description><![CDATA[Space-separated list of CSS style class(es) to be applied when this element is rendered. This value must be passed through as the "class" attribute on generated markup.]]></description>
<name>styleClass</name>
<required>no</required>
<rtexprvalue>true</rtexprvalue>
<type>java.lang.String</type>
</attribute>
<attribute>
<description><![CDATA[Position of this element in the tabbing order for the current document. This value must be an integer between 0 and 32767.]]></description>
<name>tabindex</name>
<required>no</required>
<rtexprvalue>true</rtexprvalue>
<type>java.lang.String</type>
</attribute>
<attribute>
<description><![CDATA[Advisory title information about markup elements generated for this component.]]></description>
<name>title</name>
<required>no</required>
<rtexprvalue>true</rtexprvalue>
<type>java.lang.String</type>
</attribute>
<attribute>
<description><![CDATA[MethodExpression representing a validator method that will be called during Process Validations to perform correctness checks on the value of this component. The expression must evaluate to a public method that takes FacesContext, UIComponent, and Object parameters, with a return type of void.]]></description>
<name>validator</name>
<required>no</required>
<rtexprvalue>true</rtexprvalue>
<type>javax.el.MethodExpression</type>
</attribute>
<attribute>
<description><![CDATA[If present, will be used as the text of the validator message, replacing any message that comes from the validator.]]></description>
<name>validatorMessage</name>
<required>no</required>
<rtexprvalue>true</rtexprvalue>
<type>java.lang.String</type>
</attribute>
<attribute>
<description><![CDATA[The current value of the simple component. The value to be rendered.]]></description>
<name>value</name>
<required>no</required>
<rtexprvalue>true</rtexprvalue>
<type>java.lang.Object</type>
</attribute>
<attribute>
<description><![CDATA[MethodExpression representing a value change listener method that will be notified when a new value has been set for this input component. The expression must evaluate to a public method that takes a <code>ValueChangeEvent</code> parameter, with a return type of void, or to a public method that takes no arguments with a return type of void. In the latter case, the method has no way of easily knowing what the new value is, but this can be useful in cases where a notification is needed that "this value changed".]]></description>
<name>valueChangeListener</name>
<required>no</required>
<rtexprvalue>true</rtexprvalue>
<type>javax.el.MethodExpression</type>
</attribute>
<attribute>
<description><![CDATA[Name of the widget variable to access client side api.]]></description>
<name>widgetVar</name>
<required>no</required>
<rtexprvalue>true</rtexprvalue>
<type>java.lang.String</type>
</attribute>
</tag>
<tag>
<description><![CDATA[Render a HTML &lt;canvas&rt; data visualization using a Java interface to the jqPlot charting API. A List of ChartSeries subclasses define the data and its representation in the visualization.<p>For more information, see the <a href="http://wiki.icefaces.org/display/ICE/Chart">Chart Wiki Documentation</a>.</p><hr><table border='1' cellpadding='3' cellspacing='0' width='100%'><tr bgcolor='#CCCCFF' class='TableHeadingColor'><td colspan='3'><font size='+2'><b>Client Events</b></font></td></tr><tr><td><b>Name</b></td><td><b>Description</b></td><td><b>Supported classes for argument</b></td><tr><tr><td>click</td><td>Fired when data point is clicked plot.</td><td>javax.faces.event.AjaxBehaviorEvent</td></tr><tr><td>dragStart</td><td>Fired when a drag has begun on a particular drag-enabled plot data point.</td><td>javax.faces.event.AjaxBehaviorEvent</td></tr><tr><td>dragStop</td><td>Fired when a drag has ceased on a particular drag-enabled plot data point.</td><td>javax.faces.event.AjaxBehaviorEvent</td></tr><tr><td>mouseInData</td><td>Fired when the mouse is inside a filled plot region.</td><td>javax.faces.event.AjaxBehaviorEvent</td></tr><tr><td>mouseOutData</td><td>Fired when the mouse is outside a filled plot region.</td><td>javax.faces.event.AjaxBehaviorEvent</td></tr><tr><td>showHighlighter</td><td>Fired when the highlighter is being displayed by the mouse being near an enabled data point.</td><td>javax.faces.event.AjaxBehaviorEvent</td></tr><tr><td>hideHighlighter</td><td>Fired when the highlighter is being hidden by the mouse moving away from an enabled data point.</td><td>javax.faces.event.AjaxBehaviorEvent</td></tr></table><i>Client events can be used with Client Behaviors and the ace:ajax tag.</i><br>]]></description>
<name>chart</name>
<tag-class>org.icefaces.ace.component.chart.ChartTag</tag-class>
<body-content>JSP</body-content>
<attribute>
<description><![CDATA[Enables the draw animation behaviour of the chart. By default is enabled for all browsers but IE8 and lower for performanceconcerns.]]></description>
<name>animated</name>
<required>no</required>
<rtexprvalue>true</rtexprvalue>
<type>java.lang.Boolean</type>
</attribute>
<attribute>
<description><![CDATA[Using an EL expression, bind the component reference to a bean property, so that the component may be accessed in the bean.]]></description>
<name>binding</name>
<required>no</required>
<rtexprvalue>true</rtexprvalue>
<type>javax.el.ValueExpression</type>
</attribute>
<attribute>
<description><![CDATA[Enable a crosshair cursor on the chart.]]></description>
<name>cursor</name>
<required>no</required>
<rtexprvalue>true</rtexprvalue>
<type>java.lang.Boolean</type>
</attribute>
<attribute>
<description><![CDATA[Define a Axis whose configuration is used where other axes have not made an explicit configuration.]]></description>
<name>defaultAxesConfig</name>
<required>no</required>
<rtexprvalue>true</rtexprvalue>
<type>org.icefaces.ace.component.chart.Axis</type>
</attribute>
<attribute>
<description><![CDATA[Define a ChartSeries whose configuration is used where other ChartSeries have not made an explicit configuration. The data of this ChartSeries is irrelevant. If defined, this ChartSeries should explicitly have the typefield set, this will be used as the default type for all series which have not explicitly defined a type. If undefined the default type is determined by theChartSeries.getDefaultType() of the first attached series.]]></description>
<name>defaultSeriesConfig</name>
<required>no</required>
<rtexprvalue>true</rtexprvalue>
<type>org.icefaces.ace.model.chart.ChartSeries</type>
</attribute>
<attribute>
<description><![CDATA[Define the height of the entire chart region in pixels.]]></description>
<name>height</name>
<required>no</required>
<rtexprvalue>true</rtexprvalue>
<type>java.lang.Integer</type>
</attribute>
<attribute>
<description><![CDATA[Enable the default handling of the chart when rendered into a hidden page region. Thechart polls its hidden status, looking for when it is shown, and then completes its initialization.This can be expensive in environments of reduced JavaScript performance with many charts and a complex DOM.When this is disabled, upon revealing a chart, to ensure it is correctly displayed, 'chartWidgetvar.replot()' must be called. Default = 'true'.]]></description>
<name>hiddenInitPolling</name>
<required>no</required>
<rtexprvalue>true</rtexprvalue>
<type>java.lang.Boolean</type>
</attribute>
<attribute>
<description><![CDATA[Enables drawing an info string at the cursor position when hovering at data points. Default configuration displays x, y values.]]></description>
<name>highlighter</name>
<required>no</required>
<rtexprvalue>true</rtexprvalue>
<type>java.lang.Boolean</type>
</attribute>
<attribute>
<description><![CDATA[Defines the point values passed to the highlighter tooltip, either X, Y, XY or YX. Default is XY.]]></description>
<name>highlighterAxes</name>
<required>no</required>
<rtexprvalue>true</rtexprvalue>
<type>org.icefaces.ace.component.chart.HighlighterTooltipAxes</type>
</attribute>
<attribute>
<description><![CDATA[Enables the highlighted series being temporarily reordered to be entirely visible.]]></description>
<name>highlighterBringSeriesToFront</name>
<required>no</required>
<rtexprvalue>true</rtexprvalue>
<type>java.lang.Boolean</type>
</attribute>
<attribute>
<description><![CDATA[Defines a format string populated with the x, y values indicated by the highlighterAxes. Takes C-style string format options ex. 'Date: %s, number of cats: %d' ]]></description>
<name>highlighterFormatString</name>
<required>no</required>
<rtexprvalue>true</rtexprvalue>
<type>java.lang.String</type>
</attribute>
<attribute>
<description><![CDATA[Defines the direction the highlighter tooltip is located relative to the cursor. Is 'NW' by default.]]></description>
<name>highlighterLocation</name>
<required>no</required>
<rtexprvalue>true</rtexprvalue>
<type>org.icefaces.ace.component.chart.Location</type>
</attribute>
<attribute>
<description><![CDATA[Enables drawing an 'active' styled point marker while the highlighter tooltip is shown. Is true by default.]]></description>
<name>highlighterShowMarker</name>
<required>no</required>
<rtexprvalue>true</rtexprvalue>
<type>java.lang.Boolean</type>
</attribute>
<attribute>
<description><![CDATA[Defines how many Y values a highlighter should expect in the data points array. Typically this is 1.  Certain plots, like OHLC, will have more y values in each data point array and will need this property adjusted to parse correctly.]]></description>
<name>highlighterYValueCount</name>
<required>no</required>
<rtexprvalue>true</rtexprvalue>
<type>java.lang.Integer</type>
</attribute>
<attribute>
<description><![CDATA[The component identifier for this component. This value must be unique within the closest parent component that is a naming container.]]></description>
<name>id</name>
<required>no</required>
<rtexprvalue>true</rtexprvalue>
<type>java.lang.String</type>
</attribute>
<attribute>
<description><![CDATA[MethodExpression reference called whenever an exportToServer() call is made for this chart in the client side. The method receives a single argument, ChartImageExportEvent. The bytes representing the PNG image are obtained as a byte array by calling getBytes() on the ChartImageExportEvent object.]]></description>
<name>imageExportListener</name>
<required>no</required>
<rtexprvalue>true</rtexprvalue>
<type>javax.el.MethodExpression</type>
</attribute>
<attribute>
<description><![CDATA[Enabling displays the legend.]]></description>
<name>legend</name>
<required>no</required>
<rtexprvalue>true</rtexprvalue>
<type>java.lang.Boolean</type>
</attribute>
<attribute>
<description><![CDATA[Defines the location of legend relative to the bounds of the chart. All of the cardinal directions are available in the following format: N, NE, E, SE, S, etc.]]></description>
<name>legendLocation</name>
<required>no</required>
<rtexprvalue>true</rtexprvalue>
<type>org.icefaces.ace.component.chart.Location</type>
</attribute>
<attribute>
<description><![CDATA[Defines the placement of the legend relative to the content of the chart. The available configurations are: INSIDE_GRID, OUTSIDE_GRID and OUTSIDE]]></description>
<name>legendPlacement</name>
<required>no</required>
<rtexprvalue>true</rtexprvalue>
<type>org.icefaces.ace.component.chart.LegendPlacement</type>
</attribute>
<attribute>
<description><![CDATA[MethodExpression reference called whenever a series element is dragged to a new x or y value. The method receives a single argument, PointValueChangeEvent.]]></description>
<name>pointChangeListener</name>
<required>no</required>
<rtexprvalue>true</rtexprvalue>
<type>javax.el.MethodExpression</type>
</attribute>
<attribute>
<description><![CDATA[Return true if this component (and its children) should be rendered during the Render Response phase of the request processing lifecycle. Default = 'true'.]]></description>
<name>rendered</name>
<required>no</required>
<rtexprvalue>true</rtexprvalue>
<type>boolean</type>
</attribute>
<attribute>
<description><![CDATA[MethodExpression reference called whenever a series element is selected. The method receives a single argument, SeriesSelectionEvent.]]></description>
<name>selectListener</name>
<required>no</required>
<rtexprvalue>true</rtexprvalue>
<type>javax.el.MethodExpression</type>
</attribute>
<attribute>
<description><![CDATA[Enable display of a legend regarding the coordinates of the cursor. The 'cursor' property must be enabled to use this property.]]></description>
<name>showTooltip</name>
<required>no</required>
<rtexprvalue>true</rtexprvalue>
<type>java.lang.Boolean</type>
</attribute>
<attribute>
<description><![CDATA[Enables a stack or "mountain" plot.  Not all types of series may support this mode. Default = 'false'.]]></description>
<name>stackSeries</name>
<required>no</required>
<rtexprvalue>true</rtexprvalue>
<type>java.lang.Boolean</type>
</attribute>
<attribute>
<description><![CDATA[Define CSS inline style for the chart container.]]></description>
<name>style</name>
<required>no</required>
<rtexprvalue>true</rtexprvalue>
<type>java.lang.String</type>
</attribute>
<attribute>
<description><![CDATA[Define a title of the entire chart.]]></description>
<name>title</name>
<required>no</required>
<rtexprvalue>true</rtexprvalue>
<type>java.lang.String</type>
</attribute>
<attribute>
<description><![CDATA[Define an individual instance or List of ChartSeries objects to draw on this plot.]]></description>
<name>value</name>
<required>no</required>
<rtexprvalue>true</rtexprvalue>
<type>java.lang.Object</type>
</attribute>
<attribute>
<description><![CDATA[The JavaScript global component instance name. Must be unique among components on a page. ]]></description>
<name>widgetVar</name>
<required>no</required>
<rtexprvalue>true</rtexprvalue>
<type>java.lang.String</type>
</attribute>
<attribute>
<description><![CDATA[Define the width of the entire chart region in pixels.]]></description>
<name>width</name>
<required>no</required>
<rtexprvalue>true</rtexprvalue>
<type>java.lang.Integer</type>
</attribute>
<attribute>
<description><![CDATA[Defines the configuration of the x1 axis. Attempts are made to interpret a configuration if undefined.]]></description>
<name>x2Axis</name>
<required>no</required>
<rtexprvalue>true</rtexprvalue>
<type>org.icefaces.ace.component.chart.Axis</type>
</attribute>
<attribute>
<description><![CDATA[Defines the configuration of the x axis. Attempts are made to interpret a configuration if undefined.]]></description>
<name>xAxis</name>
<required>no</required>
<rtexprvalue>true</rtexprvalue>
<type>org.icefaces.ace.component.chart.Axis</type>
</attribute>
<attribute>
<description><![CDATA[Defines the configuration of the y axes (up to 9). Attempts are made to interpret a configuration if undefined.]]></description>
<name>yAxes</name>
<required>no</required>
<rtexprvalue>true</rtexprvalue>
<type>org.icefaces.ace.component.chart.Axis[]</type>
</attribute>
<attribute>
<description><![CDATA[Enable click+drag selection of a range on the chart using the cursor. The 'cursor' property must be enabled to use this property.]]></description>
<name>zoom</name>
<required>no</required>
<rtexprvalue>true</rtexprvalue>
<type>java.lang.Boolean</type>
</attribute>
</tag>
<tag>
<description><![CDATA[TextEntry is a text input component that can display some placeholder text inside the input field when the component doesn't have a value and is not focussed. It also has custom styling for invalid state and required status.<p>For more information, see the <a href="http://wiki.icefaces.org/display/ICE/TextEntry">TextEntry Wiki Documentation</a>.<hr><table border='1' cellpadding='3' cellspacing='0' width='100%'><tr bgcolor='#CCCCFF' class='TableHeadingColor'><td colspan='3'><font size='+2'><b>Client Events</b></font></td></tr><tr><td><b>Name</b></td><td><b>Description</b></td><td><b>Supported classes for argument</b></td><tr><tr><td>blur</td><td>Fired when the text input field loses focus (default event).</td><td>javax.faces.event.AjaxBehaviorEvent</td></tr><tr><td>change</td><td>Fired when the component detects value is changed.</td><td>javax.faces.event.AjaxBehaviorEvent</td></tr></table><i>Client events can be used with Client Behaviors and the ace:ajax tag.</i><br>]]></description>
<name>textEntry</name>
<tag-class>org.icefaces.ace.component.textentry.TextEntryTag</tag-class>
<body-content>JSP</body-content>
<attribute>
<description><![CDATA[Access key that, when pressed, transfers focus to this element.]]></description>
<name>accesskey</name>
<required>no</required>
<rtexprvalue>true</rtexprvalue>
<type>java.lang.String</type>
</attribute>
